1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Skoskatten 1711 (a Hans Torgrimsen and wife was listed among labourers and crofters at Egersund; this may have been Hans Torgrimsen and Margrete Atlaksdatter):'''
2 CONT Rentekammeret inntil 1814, Reviderte regnskaper, Fogderegnskap, RA/EA-4092/R46/L2735: Fogderegnskap Jæren og Dalane, 1711, s. 290. https://www.digitalarkivet.no/rk10081305100295
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Probate record after her I husband (23-02-1705; Jens was dead and his heirs were listed as the widow, Margrete Atlaksdatter, and their son Atlak Jensen):'''
2 CONT Lister sorenskriveri, SAK/1221-0003/H/Hc/L0010: Skifteprotokoll nr 10 med register, 1704-1706, s. 54b-55a. https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk20081029350340
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Probate record of her parents (23-06-1712; Both parents were still alive when they surrendered their estate to their children, which included Margrete, married to Hans Torgrimsen Hadland):'''
2 CONT Jæren og Dalane sorenskriveri, SAST/A-100306/5/50BA/L0004: SKIFTEPROTOKOLL, 1708-1714, s. 318b-319a. https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk20081106660620
2 CONT
2 CONT ---- 
2 CONT Both "Lunds historie" ([https://www.nb.no/items/931a4ffb452f6a2306de08a17b4d6987?page=460 p.459] and [https://www.nb.no/items/931a4ffb452f6a2306de08a17b4d6987?page=172 pp.171-172]) and "Bygdebok for Nes herred" ([https://www.nb.no
2 CONC /items/a04d6f46f9287e53fce52f5481798c4f?page=113&searchText=%22Atlak%20Jensson%22 pp.110-111]) state that 'Jens Larsen Gursli' was married to 'Margrete Atlaksdatter Hove', who was the widow after 'Hans Torgrimsen Hadland'. This ca
2 CONC n't be correct, as 'Jens Larsen Gursli' died before [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk20081029350340 his probate dated 23-02-1705], while 'Margrete' and 'Hans' were listed as married in the [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk20081106
2 CONC 660620 probate of her parents, dated 23-06-1712]. Thus,''' 'Margrete' must have been married to 'Jens' first, living at Nes, and then to 'Hans', living at Egersund'''. This also helps explain why her son, 'Atlak Jensen' is later r
2 CONC eported as living at Sæstad, Egersund.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Is there any '''evidence''' supporting the claim that Margrete died 1738? There does not appear to be such an entry in the church records at Egersund.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
