2 DATE 27 NOV 1920
2 ADDR
3 CITY Plymouth
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tollak Osmundsen var på besøk i Norge i 1909. Då var han 82 år gamal. I passasjerlista for reisa tilbake til USA er fødestedet Sirdal, bostedet Elroy i Juneau, Wisconsin. Kontaktperson i Norge er søstera Elisabeth 
2 CONC Tjensvold og kontaktperson i USA er sonen Ivar Tollagsen. Skipet gjekk frå Kristiansand 27 mars. Elisabeth døydde 16. mars og blei gravlagd 22. mars det året.
2 CONT
2 CONT Teksten under er tatt fra [https://digitalcommons.andrews.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1145&context=pubs Juneau County, Wisconsin Bygdebok: A Genealogy of the Norwegian Settlers, 1850-1950 av Larry Onsager]. (Navnet på far til 
2 CONC kona er feil her, skal være Tjøstolv Iversen og ikkje Iver Tjøstolvsen) 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Osmundson, Tallak Tostad s of Osmund Osmundson (see) and Turi Talleksdtr.
2 CONT Tallak was born on July 24, 1824 (1826, Dec Int, March 1832, 1900 cen) in Sirdal
2 CONT (Lirdal), Toustad, Norway. He emigrated in 1872, entering Quebec in July. Tallak was
2 CONT married in Plymouth Township by Rev. Brynjolf Hovde on January 11, 1875 to Dorthea
2 CONT Iversdtr. Aarthun. He was a farmer living in Fountain Township. The witnesses were Ole O.
2 CONT Kjerntvedt and Anders Osmundsen.
2 CONT Dorthea, the dau of Iver Tjostrvsen (see Everson, Chester) and Ingeborg
2 CONT Osmundsdtr., was born in March 1854 (January 1856, 1900 cen) in Sovde (Lovde),
2 CONT Toustad, Norway. She emigrated in 1869. In 1880, Tallak and Dorthea lived on a farm in
2 CONT Fountain Township. Tallak declared his intent to become a naturalized citizen on October 1,
2 CONT 1880 in Juneau County. Tallak and Dorthea joined the Fountain Church on October 24,
2 CONT 1882. In 1900 and 1905, they lived on a farm in Plymouth Township. Dorthea died on
2 CONT August 31, 1903 in Fountain Township and was buried on September 2, 1903. Tallak died
2 CONT on November 27, 1920 in Plymouth Township and was buried on November 30, 1920
2 CONT (ELCR; FCR; US Cen, 1880, Fountain Twp #45, 1900, Plymouth #45; Wis Cen, 1905,
2 CONT Plymouth #118).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT Olaus Severin, b. Feb 13, 1876, WI; bp. Apr 14, 1876 (spon: Ole Johnsen, Siri
2 CONT Osmundsen, Martin Simonsen, Ragnild Olsdtr., Kolbein Gabrielsen, and
2 CONT Ingeborg Tjostovsdtr.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Iver Theodor, b. Dec 12, 1877, WI; bp. Dec 26, 1877 (spon: Ole Kjerntvedt, Even E.
2 CONT Osteraa, Torbjor Osteraa, Halvor O. Juve, Martha Juve, and Matta Kalhagen);
2 CONT conf, Jul 17, 1890, FLC, Iver Thompson, laborer, 1905.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olava Antonine, b. Feb 20, 1880, WI; bp. May 2, 1880, E Lem (spon: Ole
2 CONT Kjerntvedt, Ole Kalhagen, Lina Nilsdtr., Martin Tollefsen, Kari Evensen, and
2 CONT Martha Juve); conf, Aug 12, 1894, FLC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Oskar, b. Jul 1, 1883; bp. Jul 29, 1883, Fountain (spon: Ole Johnsen, Nils
2 CONT Syvertsen, Anders Osmundsen, Siri Johnsen, Ingeborg Osmundsen, and Elen
2 CONT Moklev).
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaus Severin, b. Nov 14, 1886; bp. May 22, 1887, Fountain (spon: Ole & Sigri
2 CONT Johnson, Kari Osmundson, Helge Juve, and Clara Vetrhus).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Onsager, Lawrence W., "Juneau County, Wisconsin Bygdebok: A Genealogy of the Norwegian Settlers, 1850-1950" (2013). Faculty
2 CONT Publications. 146.''
2 CONT ''https://digitalcommons.andrews.edu/pubs/146''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
