1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I følge Juneau County, Wisconsin Bygdebok bodde han i Juneau County, Wisconsin. Samme county som broren Tollak. Om dødsdatoen er korrekt døde han før broren kom over
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Osmundsen, Ole son of Osmund Osmundsen and Tori Tallaksdtr. Ole was married on August 28, 1863 in Lindina Township to Siri (Jeri) Osmundsdtr. The witnesses were Knud Leone and Ole Berenson. Siri was the daughter of Osmund Andersen
2 CONC  Kjerntvedt  and Marthe Olsdtr. She was the sister of Ole Sondenaa Osmundsen (Spring Prairie Church record, pp. 42-43). Ole and Siri joined the Lemonweir Church in October 1863. Ole’s name is crossed out which would indicated that
2 CONC  he had moved or died. Siri’s name is not crossed out (ELCR, v. , members #112 & 113). Possibly Ole was the Civil War soldier who died in 1864? Ole Osmundsen, a resident of Lindina Township, Juneau County, Wisconsin, enlisted on N
2 CONC ovember 17, 1863 in Company E, 1st Wisconsin Infantry Regiment. He was wounded on August 8, 1864 and died on August 11, 1864 (Roster of Wis Vols, War of Rebellion, 886)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Onsager, Lawrence W., "[https://digitalcommons.andrews.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1145&context=pubs Juneau County, Wisconsin Bygdebok]: A Genealogy of the Norwegian Settlers, 1850-1950" (2013). Faculty Publications. 146.''
2 CONT
